course: dictionary
lesson: 11559
title: Comparing with analogous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Analogous is a word for things that are alike in some way, so that you can compare them. Its sound is a clue: it is related to analogy, which means a comparison. «The heart is analogous to a pump, because both push fluid around.» You do not need to know how a heart works. The words analogous to tell you the two things are being compared.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «My plan is analogous to a recipe: follow the steps and you get the result.» The sentence compares a plan with a recipe, so analogous means they are alike in some way. Swap in a simpler word: "My plan is similar to a recipe" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Scientists use analogous when two things do the same job but developed in different ways. «A bird's wing and an insect's wing are analogous: both help the animal fly.» The two wings are built differently, yet they share the same purpose. Analogous things are alike in use or role, even if they are not made the same way.
fact: Analogous is an adjective, and it is often followed by to: «analogous to».
fact: Analogous means similar in some way, so that it can be compared.
fact: «The heart is analogous to a pump.» A heart and a pump both move fluid.
fact: In biology, analogous parts do the same job but evolved differently, like bird and insect wings.
fact: A good check is to swap in "similar to" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The heart is analogous to a pump.» What does analogous mean here? | Heavy and difficult to lift | *Similar in some way, so they can be compared | Completely different in every way | Hidden underground
exercise: «A bird's wing and an insect's wing are analogous: both help the animal fly.» What do they share? | They are both made of metal | *The same job, even though they developed differently | They are found in the same place | They look exactly the same
exercise: Jayden says analogous means "the same as". What is the best reply? | Yes, it means the opposite | Yes, it means exactly the same | *No, it means similar in some way, so things can be compared | No, it means very heavy
test: «Our school rules are analogous to the rules of a game: both keep everyone fair.» What is being compared? | Two things that are never alike | A school and a shop | *Two things that are alike in some way | The rules and a ball
test: «A ticket is analogous to a key: each one lets you in.» What is the best meaning of analogous here? | Covered in feathers | Written down carefully | Very large | *Alike in purpose, so they can be compared
exam: Which sentence uses analogous correctly? | *A torch is analogous to a lamp, since both give light | I felt analogous and ate my lunch | The analogous ran to the shop at noon | The bus is analogous to a sleepy bear
